WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.666 --> 00:00:31.375
<b>In the previous verses,</b>

2
00:00:31.375 --> 00:00:32.708
<b>Lord Krishna explained</b>

3
00:00:32.708 --> 00:00:34.791
<b>how a person should live by performing sacrifices,</b>

4
00:00:34.791 --> 00:00:37.875
<b>offering their actions as oblations,</b>

5
00:00:37.875 --> 00:00:46.458
<b>and maintaining a relationship of cooperation</b>
<b>with the forces and deities of the universe.</b>

6
00:00:46.458 --> 00:00:53.750
<b>Now, in this verse, Lord Krishna concludes </b>
<b>this topic of sacrifice or offering.</b>

7
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:58.583
<b>He describes the fate of a person </b>
<b>who does not live in this way</b>

8
00:00:58.583 --> 00:01:04.500
<b>and fails to perform their duties and sacrifices.</b>

9
00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:11.541
<b>In this verse, Lord Krishna states</b>

10
00:01:11.541 --> 00:01:15.125
<b>that a person who does not perform </b>
<b>sacrifices according to the Vedic system,</b>

11
00:01:15.125 --> 00:01:19.208
<b>does not offer their actions as oblations,</b>

12
00:01:19.208 --> 00:01:23.208
<b>and does not offer the deities </b>
<b>the tribute of these oblations,</b>

13
00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:27.083
<b>must face the consequences.</b>

14
00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:30.250
<b>Such a person's life is without purpose.</b>

15
00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:33.500
<b>They are completely partaking in sin</b>

16
00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:37.708
<b>because they are living solely</b>
<b>for their own satisfaction.</b>

17
00:01:37.708 --> 00:01:41.083
<b>Moreover, they have forgotten gratitude.</b>

18
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:45.416
<b>The universe and the deities have generously </b>
<b>provided them with all the facilities,</b>

19
00:01:45.416 --> 00:01:48.625
<b>but they are not repaying their debt.</b>

20
00:01:48.625 --> 00:01:53.625
<b>Instead, they are stealing these facilities for free.</b>

21
00:01:53.625 --> 00:01:54.583
<b>Therefore,</b>

22
00:01:54.583 --> 00:01:56.750
<b>Lord Krishna concludes</b>

23
00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:58.583
<b>that sacrifice is essential,</b>

24
00:01:58.583 --> 00:02:02.541
<b>and offering one's actions </b>
<b>as oblations is mandatory.</b>

25
00:02:02.541 --> 00:02:04.625
<b>If someone does not do so,</b>

26
00:02:04.625 --> 00:02:10.500
<b>it is certain that they will be </b>
<b>attracted to sinful behavior.</b>

27
00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.541
<b>But why?</b>

28
00:02:12.541 --> 00:02:16.083
<b>The reason is selfishness.</b>

29
00:02:16.083 --> 00:02:17.291
<b>In sacrifice,</b>

30
00:02:17.291 --> 00:02:18.500
<b>in offering,</b>

31
00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:22.500
<b>In sacrifice, in offering, in action as </b>
<b>renunciation, there is gratitude.</b>

32
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:29.166
<b>There is a spirit of cooperation with others, staying </b>
<b>away from personal pleasure and indulgence.</b>

33
00:02:29.166 --> 00:02:34.083
<b>Not doing so is undoubtedly a selfish mentality.</b>

34
00:02:34.083 --> 00:02:37.291
<b>Selfishness never allows a person to be content;</b>

35
00:02:37.291 --> 00:02:42.833
<b>it only provokes them to </b>
<b>accumulate more and more.</b>

36
00:02:42.833 --> 00:02:43.916
<b>And then</b>

37
00:02:43.916 --> 00:02:49.416
<b>the time is not far when this very person starts </b>
<b>violating the rights of others</b>

38
00:02:49.416 --> 00:02:52.250
<b>and lays hands on their possessions.</b>

39
00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:54.500
<b>This is certainly sin.</b>

40
00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.458
<b>For this reason,</b>

41
00:02:55.458 --> 00:02:59.750
<b>if such a person does not change </b>
<b>their perspective in time,</b>

42
00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:05.375
<b>their life will surely become sinful and aimless.</b>

43
00:03:05.375 --> 00:03:09.291
<b>Spiritual upliftment is the purpose of human life.</b>

44
00:03:09.291 --> 00:03:13.875
<b>Rising above selfishness is paramount for this.</b>

45
00:03:13.875 --> 00:03:14.916
<b>Sacrifice,</b>

46
00:03:14.916 --> 00:03:21.125
<b>selfless action, and the </b>
<b>resulting spiritual upliftment –</b>

47
00:03:21.125 --> 00:03:28.791
<b>only those who follow this </b>
<b> cycle will achieve their purpose.</b>

48
00:03:33.666 --> 00:03:37.000
<b>People are becoming increasingly rare,</b>

49
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:45.125
<b>who live for the welfare of others or </b>
<b>for the upliftment of humanity.</b>

50
00:03:45.125 --> 00:03:50.541
<b>These days, most people think </b>
<b>only about their self-interest</b>

51
00:03:50.541 --> 00:03:55.000
<b>and are more interested in pleasure </b>
<b>and enjoyment than in responsibility.</b>

52
00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.375
<b>As long as they don't face personal inconvenience</b>

53
00:03:58.375 --> 00:04:01.083
<b>and their lives go smoothly,</b>

54
00:04:01.083 --> 00:04:07.500
<b>they don't care if others are living in misery</b>
<b>and poverty due to a lack of cooperation.</b>

55
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:08.791
<b>So what?</b>

56
00:04:08.791 --> 00:04:13.875
<b>It's easy to turn a blind eye to their plight, isn't it?</b>

57
00:04:13.875 --> 00:04:17.208
<b>Now ask yourself,</b>

58
00:04:17.208 --> 00:04:21.291
<b>how will you respect life?</b>

59
00:04:21.291 --> 00:04:25.000
<b>Whom will you regard with respect?</b>

60
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.375
<b>Those</b>

61
00:04:26.375 --> 00:04:30.416
<b>who remained engrossed in </b>
<b>personal indulgence and pleasure,</b>

62
00:04:30.416 --> 00:04:31.416
<b>or</b>

63
00:04:31.416 --> 00:04:39.583
<b>those who contributed to the upliftment</b>
<b>of others' lives and lived a meaningful life?</b>

64
00:04:39.583 --> 00:04:44.166
<b>Which life is worth remembering?</b>

65
00:04:44.166 --> 00:04:46.166
<b>There are countless examples before you.</b>

66
00:04:46.166 --> 00:04:51.125
<b>Only those will be remembered with respect,</b>

67
00:04:51.125 --> 00:04:55.708
<b>who made a meaningful </b>
<b>contribution to others' lives</b>

68
00:04:55.708 --> 00:05:00.041
<b>and strived for human welfare.</b>

69
00:05:00.041 --> 00:05:05.041
<b>who led a selfish life filled </b>
<b>with indulgence and luxury,</b>

70
00:05:05.041 --> 00:05:09.416
<b>no one remembers them with respect.</b>

71
00:05:09.416 --> 00:05:11.416
<b>Now make a choice.</b>

72
00:05:11.416 --> 00:05:15.208
<b>How do you want to be remembered?</b>

73
00:05:15.208 --> 00:05:18.666
<b>As a selfish, egotistical person,</b>

74
00:05:18.666 --> 00:05:19.666
<b>or</b>

75
00:05:19.666 --> 00:05:26.375
<b>as a human being who lived a </b>
<b>purposeful life, remained selfless,</b>

76
00:05:26.375 --> 00:05:29.291
<b>and contributed to human welfare?</b>

77
00:05:29.291 --> 00:05:35.250
<b>If you want to live a life of mere </b>
<b>indulgence, luxury, and pleasure,</b>

78
00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:37.708
<b>that path is open.</b>

79
00:05:37.708 --> 00:05:41.833
<b>Certainly, millions of people live such a life.</b>

80
00:05:41.833 --> 00:05:43.791
<b>The only difference is that</b>

81
00:05:43.791 --> 00:05:50.708
<b>no one will remember such a </b>
<b>life and personality with respect.</b>

82
00:05:50.708 --> 00:05:52.375
<b>Ultimately,</b>

83
00:05:52.375 --> 00:05:55.166
<b>the choice is yours,</b>

84
00:05:55.166 --> 00:06:03.291
<b>but the hope is that you will want </b>
<b>to live a memorable, purposeful life.</b>

85
00:06:03.291 --> 00:06:06.000
<b>To do this, adopt the path of duty,</b>

86
00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.166
<b>live with gratitude,</b>

87
00:06:08.166 --> 00:06:14.041
<b>and perform your actions with </b>
<b>a spirit of service to others.</b>

88
00:06:14.041 --> 00:06:15.458
<b>Think about it.</b>

89
00:06:19.291 --> 00:06:26.833
<b>We all want our families to live a comfortable life.</b>

90
00:06:26.833 --> 00:06:37.333
<b>We constantly strive to arrange every </b>
<b>possible joy of life for our loved ones.</b>

91
00:06:37.333 --> 00:06:40.875
<b>This thinking is not bad at all.</b>

92
00:06:40.875 --> 00:06:47.208
<b>It is a very natural expression of</b>
<b>your love for your dear ones.</b>

93
00:06:47.208 --> 00:06:49.041
<b>However, </b>

94
00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:52.250
<b>if this concern and care</b>

95
00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:58.125
<b>are limited only to material </b>
<b>pleasure and physical comfort,</b>

96
00:06:58.125 --> 00:07:06.125
<b>then certainly such a life will arouse </b>
<b>the tendency of indulgence and selfishness,</b>

97
00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:10.541
<b>which will ultimately entrap one in the web of sin.</b>

98
00:07:10.541 --> 00:07:11.875
<b>It is necessary</b>

99
00:07:11.875 --> 00:07:18.416
<b>that along with material comfort and joy,</b>
<b>loved ones and children</b>

100
00:07:18.416 --> 00:07:28.083
<b>are also taught the values of living with gratitude </b>
<b>and serving others with a spirit of sacrifice.</b>

101
00:07:28.083 --> 00:07:33.833
<b>The meaning of sacrifice is not just offering </b>
<b>materials into the fire.</b>

102
00:07:33.833 --> 00:07:43.666
<b>Whenever you do something good for </b>
<b>others by renouncing selfishness and ego,</b>

103
00:07:43.666 --> 00:07:46.416
<b>that is also a sacrifice.</b>

104
00:07:46.416 --> 00:07:50.083
<b>Whenever you do not compete for resources,</b>

105
00:07:50.083 --> 00:07:52.416
<b>do not merely hoard them,</b>

106
00:07:52.416 --> 00:07:53.333
<b>but</b>

107
00:07:53.333 --> 00:07:56.291
<b>share them with others,</b>

108
00:07:56.291 --> 00:07:59.041
<b>that is also renunciation.</b>

109
00:07:59.041 --> 00:08:02.708
<b>And people who live this way</b>

110
00:08:02.708 --> 00:08:08.125
<b>always have sweet and </b>
<b>meaningful relationships in society.</b>

111
00:08:08.125 --> 00:08:14.375
<b>Isn't that what you would want for your children, </b>
<b>for your loved ones –</b>

112
00:08:14.375 --> 00:08:17.666
<b>that their relationships remain joyful,</b>

113
00:08:17.666 --> 00:08:18.583
<b>sweet,</b>

114
00:08:18.583 --> 00:08:20.708
<b>and meaningful?</b>

115
00:08:20.708 --> 00:08:23.250
<b>For this, ensure</b>

116
00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:29.458
<b>that the family develops not only materially </b>
<b>but also spiritually.</b>

117
00:08:29.458 --> 00:08:32.750
<b>The children should get all the facilities,</b>

118
00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:33.833
<b>but</b>

119
00:08:33.833 --> 00:08:40.333
<b>they should not hesitate to share these </b>
<b>facilities with someone in need.</b>

120
00:08:40.333 --> 00:08:47.625
<b>This is the meaning of a </b>
<b>meaningful family and social life.</b>

121
00:08:47.625 --> 00:08:49.375
<b>Think about it.</b>

122
00:08:54.041 --> 00:09:00.833
<b>In any organization, ethics and </b>
<b>values flow from top to bottom.</b>

123
00:09:00.833 --> 00:09:03.916
<b>If the purpose of a business</b>

124
00:09:03.916 --> 00:09:07.791
<b>and the purpose of the people leading it</b>

125
00:09:07.791 --> 00:09:11.875
<b>has become solely to accumulate financial gain,</b>

126
00:09:11.875 --> 00:09:18.625
<b>then it is no wonder that unethical practices </b>
<b>will thrive in such an organization.</b>

127
00:09:18.625 --> 00:09:25.416
<b>If the purpose of the leaders has been</b>
<b>only profit and self-interest,</b>

128
00:09:25.416 --> 00:09:27.875
<b>then slowly and surely</b>

129
00:09:27.875 --> 00:09:32.583
<b>this will become the mentality of the</b>
<b>people working in the organization as well.</b>

130
00:09:32.583 --> 00:09:37.291
<b>Everyone will work only for personal gain.</b>

131
00:09:37.291 --> 00:09:42.833
<b>There will be a race for credit for any good work,</b>

132
00:09:42.833 --> 00:09:47.583
<b>but people will hesitate to </b>
<b>come forward for improvement.</b>

133
00:09:47.583 --> 00:09:52.000
<b>There will be a lack of </b>
<b>mutual cooperation and respect.</b>

134
00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:58.416
<b>And no large organization can function without </b>
<b>cooperation and respect among colleagues.</b>

135
00:09:58.416 --> 00:10:03.750
<b>Nor can such an organization</b>
<b>keep its customers satisfied.</b>

136
00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:08.333
<b>Such a business is certainly on </b>
<b>the path to disintegration.</b>

137
00:10:08.333 --> 00:10:09.416
<b>Moreover,</b>

138
00:10:09.416 --> 00:10:13.791
<b>businesses that do not hesitate to </b>
<b>destroy the environment,</b>

139
00:10:13.791 --> 00:10:17.916
<b>do not shy away from </b>
<b>exploiting natural resources,</b>

140
00:10:17.916 --> 00:10:23.416
<b>the mental health of the people </b>
<b>working there on the back burner</b>

141
00:10:23.416 --> 00:10:28.541
<b>and focus only and only on profit while keeping,</b>

142
00:10:28.541 --> 00:10:33.250
<b>such businesses quickly lose their purpose.</b>

143
00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:35.666
<b>Economic profit is necessary,</b>

144
00:10:35.666 --> 00:10:39.708
<b>it is a major objective of any business,</b>

145
00:10:39.708 --> 00:10:44.916
<b>but at the same time every organization, </b>
<b>the people leading it,</b>

146
00:10:44.916 --> 00:10:47.083
<b>will have to introspect</b>

147
00:10:47.083 --> 00:10:54.625
<b>on how they are contributing to </b>
<b>making human life easier, what their purpose is.</b>

148
00:10:54.625 --> 00:10:57.916
<b>If natural resources are being used,</b>

149
00:10:57.916 --> 00:11:03.791
<b>then in return what contribution </b>
<b>can be made for environmental conservation?</b>

150
00:11:03.791 --> 00:11:11.166
<b>If people are working tirelessly, are they being </b>
<b>given respect and facilities?Z</b>

151
00:11:11.166 --> 00:11:14.791
<b>This self-reflection is necessary.</b>

152
00:11:14.791 --> 00:11:17.041
<b>Think about it.</b>

